## Slide structure

> **31 slides total (live deck): 24 main-session slides + 7 standalone Stitching Prototypes extension slides.**
> **Pending, not yet in the live deck:** a new "Step 1 of 6: Clean up your design file" slide, which pushes the Build section from 5 steps to 6 (see flagged entry below) — once built, the main session becomes 25 slides / 32 total.
> The main session compresses the lesson's Phase 2 ("Starting fresh" chat-prompt steps) and Phase 4 (MCP build steps) into one continuous Section 04 — there is no separate "generate the pattern via chat prompts" section in this deck. Students go straight from defining the two layers conceptually (Section 03) into building via MCP (Section 04: scope → sync tokens → component inventory → interaction pattern → build one screen at a time → refine → expectations).
> There are no separate Milestone/timer slides and no separate "Reflect" section slide in this deck — the closing slide (24) serves as both wrap-up and reflection prompt. Instructors should run Phase 4 hands-on time and Phase 5 share-and-reflect off this same closing context rather than expecting dedicated slides.
> The Stitching Prototypes extension (slides 25–31) is a self-contained 7-slide module, consistent with the lesson file's instruction to run it as a separate standalone session, optional reading, or one-sentence mention — it is not folded into the 24-slide main count.

